# Start a managed single-arm teleoperation session (motion.arm.session_start).
#
# Pose commands on motion.arm.pose are clutch_relative: each one is a
# displacement and a base-frame rotation delta from the clutch origin returned
# here. The origin is the runtime's command-side reference (the end-effector
# target it is holding), not the measured pose, so gravity sag is not taken
# into the origin. The runtime replaces the reference with the measured pose
# only when no valid reference exists or when the two differ by more than its
# reset threshold; reference_reset reports that.
#
# Pose and lease messages stamped at or before the session start are dropped,
# so late messages from an earlier session cannot act on this one.
---
bool success
string message
# Clutch origin of this session in the base frame; header.stamp is the
# session start time.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped reference
# m; distance between the reference and the measured end-effector position at
# start. NaN when success is false.
float64 position_error_m
# True when the reference was (re)built from the measured pose for this session.
bool reference_reset
